#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""arch-update-ui: full-screen, animated front-end for arch-update  (by Cactus)

Splash with the gradient ARCH UPDATE title, update check + Arch news, an
arrow-key menu, an in-app news reader, settings (the update reports, off until
the user says yes; restarting the services by itself; the last updates kept on
this machine, each one's report to look at, send or delete), a compact live
dashboard while the update runs (stages, progress, ETA learned from previous
runs), a modal for questions that need a human, and a summary screen with the
system checks and what can be done about them: send this update's report,
restart the services it left waiting, fix the problems with booting it found.
Until such problems are fixed or the machine rebooted, the menu warns about them.

The update itself is run by the shared engine (lib/engine.py next to this
program): real arch-update in a pty, routine questions answered, risky ones
handed to you, every run logged to ~/.local/state/arch-update-auto/logs/.

  arch-update-ui           normal use (started by the tray icon / launcher)
  arch-update-ui --demo    the whole show on a simulated update (changes nothing)
  arch-update-ui --self-test   draw every screen off-screen (used before a self-update is accepted)
"""
